  "body": "**What happens:** on a lathe whose machine file states **no C travel and no C rate** (e.g. the `c_axis_live` test bench), `fanuc-lathe.cps` still posts C-turning rapids (the C-section links) with an F word that has no cap, the same unstated feed #906 refuses when a C travel *is* stated. That behaviour predates #860, and #906 (PR #964) left it out of scope. It is noted in `docs/decisions/906-c-unwind-rate-cap.md`.\n\n**Expected:** a C-section move that turns C on a machine that states no C rate is refused by name, the same as #906's refusal, or else posted without an invented F. It is never posted at an uncapped feed the control has to clamp.\n\n**Related:** #906 / PR #964 (C travel stated, no rate); #885 (fanuc.cps / doosan-dnm.cps combined linear + C moves at the mill feed). This issue covers the lathe post with neither travel nor rate stated.\n\n**Done means:** posting a C-turning op on a machine with no C rate either refuses by name or posts no uncapped F; pinned through the lathe post on the `c_axis_live` bench; any goldens that move are listed.\n\nFound by the #906 worker (SKULL).\n",
